WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.5 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Safeguarding

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Safeguarding starts with your very first activity, including pilots, even in a team of two.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Safeguarding means protecting people, especially children and adults at risk, from harm caused by your team, partners, programmes or operations. It applies from your very first activity, including pilots and online work.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Safe practice in three moments

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.981
Before: Vetting, training, consent and a risk check for each activity. For example: Consent from a parent or carer for 17-year-olds, and a kitchen safety check before the pilot.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:51.052
During: Two adults present, clear roles and a named focal person on site. For example: Two adults are always present with trainees in the kitchen, and one founder is focal person.

7
00:00:51.052 --> 00:01:05.063
If a concern arises: Listen, do not investigate, tell the lead the same day and refer as the procedure says. For example: A mentor tells the focal founder, who follows the referral route agreed before launch.

8
00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:06.063
Why it comes first

9
00:01:06.063 --> 00:01:12.107
1. Harm to someone you serve is the most serious risk you face.

10
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:17.781
2. Even a team of two can cause harm, or miss it.

11
00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:25.196
3. Families and partners trust you only if you protect people from day one.

12
00:01:25.596 --> 00:01:26.196
What your framework includes

13
00:01:26.196 --> 00:01:32.981
1. A policy, code of conduct, a lead, a deputy and someone outside the founders.

14
00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:38.285
2. Safer recruitment, training and safe activity design, including online rules.

15
00:01:38.285 --> 00:01:45.330
3. A way to report, record, refer and support, checked locally every year.

16
00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.330
What to avoid

17
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:52.004
Waiting until after pilots or trial sessions to set it up.

18
00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:56.937
Writing procedures without qualified local advice and referral contacts.

19
00:01:56.937 --> 00:02:02.130
Recording confidential case details in this workspace.

20
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.530
You outline your safeguarding framework, without case details.

21
00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.530
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.130
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
